"Dr Mundo": First, what makes Neon different from Sodium and Chlorine?

Player: <Empty Text Event>

- Neon already has a full outer electron shell.
	"Dr Mundo": Exactly!
	
	"Dr Mundo": Neon has the electron arrangement 2,8. Its outermost energy level contains eight electrons, making it complete.
	
	"Dr Mundo": This is why Neon is generally very stable and does not readily react with other atoms.
	
