"Dr Mundo": Now let's compare Sodium and Chlorine.

"Dr Mundo": Sodium has the electron arrangement 2,8,1, while Chlorine has 2,8,7.

"Dr Mundo": What could Sodium do to achieve a full outer shell?

Player: <Empty Text Event>

- Lose one electron.
	"Dr Mundo": Correct!
	
	"Dr Mundo": "Dr Mundo"\: When Sodium loses its outermost electron, its remaining electrons have the arrangement 2,8.
	
	"Dr Mundo": It forms a positively charged ion called Na+.
	
